mapping "V2250.1" source="V2250" target="10298002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V2250 = Swedish 5-char extension of ICD-10 V22.5 (Motorcycle rider [passenger] injured in
        collision with two- or three-wheeled motor vehicle, traffic accident), with 5th char SNOMED CT
        10298002 = idrott/sport/motion activity context. Athena ICD10 mirror crosswalk for base V22.5
        (concept 45565957) maps to SNOMED CT 438310 (Victim, motorcycle rider in vehicular AND/OR traffic
        accident, code 10298002), 434228 (Passenger in vehicular accident), and 4053423 (MV on road in
        collision with motorcycle). 438310 chosen as strongest single target: it captures the
        motorcyclist-injury semantic shared by all V22/V23 base codes. Broader because the Swedish
        activity-context axis (sport/work/etc.) has no SNOMED CT representation and is lost; target fully
        contains the injury semantics. Moderate tier : mechanical Athena crosswalk from the base V22.5,
        not independently re-verified for the Swedish extension; activity-context loss is acceptable
        lossy-ness rather than a defect.
        """
}
